  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following is not a condensation polymer?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Nylon<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Nylon<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Dacron",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Buna<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>S</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(a) Nylon<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;is the polymer of hexamethylene diamine and adipic acid. It is made by the condensation of given monomers.</p><p>(b) Nylon<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;os also a condensation polymer of caprolactum. It is a polymide.</p><p>(c) Dacron is also a condensation polymer of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid. It is an example of polyester.</p><p>(d) Buna<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;is an addition polymer of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;butadiene and styrene.</p><p>Hence, only (4) is not a condensation polymer.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;(4) is the correct option.</p>"
  }
}